WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:08.000
Who, or what is an impostor?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.200
Simple definition: a person who deceives others by pretending to be someone else

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.100
Full definition:
one that assumes false identity or title for

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.250
the purpose of deception

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:25.449
Wow, the full definition is a whopping 7 characters
more. I don't even know what to do with this

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:30.420
amount of time I saved reading the simple
definition first.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.130
Let's look in the mind of someone who suffers
from impostor syndrome and see the fickle

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.149
understanding they have of their own achievements.

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:44.280
98 points out of 100, this surely means that they
mixed up my submission with someone else's,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.500
who was way smarter than I am.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.329
I went in for the next round of interviews,
messed up big time, and I got hired with an

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:56.949
incredible salary. This can, of course, only
be a misunderstanding.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:01:01.430
I got elected for this prestigious award.
I don't know how this could possibly have

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:06.210
happened. Maybe someone who really likes me
tried to pressure the prize committee to vote

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.710
for me. I cannot possibly imagine any other
way of this happening.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:18.320
I've been 5 years at the company now and still, no one found out that I am a fraud. That's a disaster

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.880
Nothing can be convince me that I am not an
impostor who fooled everyone else for being

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.070
a bright person.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.860
However funny as it may sound, this is a very
real problem.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.880
Researchers, academics and high achieving
women are especially vulnerable to this condition.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.610
But it is indeed not limited to these professions.
For instance, Hayden Christensen, the actor

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:44.790
playing Anakin Skywalker in the beloved Star
Wars series appears to suffer from very similar

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:45.229
symptoms.

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:48.710
He said:
"I felt like I had this great thing in Star

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:53.590
Wars that provided all these opportunities
and gave me a career, but it all kind of felt

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.090
a little too handed to me," he explained.
"I didn't want to go through life feeling

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.320
like I was just riding a wave."

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:08.700
So, as a response, he hasn't really done any
acting for 4 years.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.900
He said:
‘If this time away is gonna be damaging

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.910
to my career, then so be it. If I can come
back afterward and claw my way back in, then

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.660
maybe I’ll feel like I earned it.'”

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.790
The treatment of impostor syndrome includes
group sittings where the patients discuss

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.540
their lives and come to a sudden realization
that they are not alone and this this not

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.700
an individual case but a common pattern
among high achieving people. As they are also

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.989
very keen on dismissing praise and kind words,
they are instructed to be more vigilant about

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:43.840
doing that, and try to take in all the nourishment
they get from their colleagues. These are

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:52.750
the more common ways to treat this serious
condition that poisons so many people's minds.

